    "answer": "An active backlog is a course a student has failed and not yet cleared, while a cleared backlog (history of arrears) is a course failed once and passed later [1]. Unless a company specifies otherwise, company criteria refer to active backlogs [1]. Students must report their backlog status honestly, as a wrong declaration leads to debarment under section 10 [1]. \n\nCompany-specific backlog eligibility criteria for 2027 graduates are as follows:\n- Veltrix Systems allows no active backlogs and no more than one cleared backlog [2].\n- LumenGrid Energy allows no active backlogs at the time of applying [3].\n- Nimbusware Technologies permits at most 1 active backlog at the time of applying, which must be cleared before joining [4].\n- Quantaleaf Analytics allows at most 1 active backlog [5].",
